cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness, please cite it."
title: "mhh-gate: an executable pre-registration harness for frame-history experiments on GR00T N1.7"
abstract: >-
  A gate runner that turns a pre-registration into code. Every guarantee a fair
  comparison depends on is asserted at the point it could fail silently, and a
  violation aborts the run rather than printing a warning: the wrong checkpoint
  aborts, an edited episode list aborts because the list is hashed at
  pre-registration time, no best-checkpoint selection exists anywhere in the
  codebase, and extra episodes from unseeded autoreset are flagged per task
  rather than folded into an aggregate.
authors:
  - family-names: Chillara
    given-names: Mohan
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohanchillara1/mhh-gate"
type: software
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - vision-language-action
  - LIBERO
  - robot learning
